    <Folder>
      <name>Intelligence Summary</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>AI Council Assessment</name>
        <styleUrl>#intel</styleUrl>
        <description>The synthesized intelligence reveals a deliberate U.S. military posture focused on deterring Iranian aggression in the Strait of Hormuz while maintaining strategic flexibility in the Indo-Pacific. The deployment of USS Abraham Lincoln (CVN-72) to the Indian Ocean and USS George Washington (CVN-73) to the Persian Gulf underscores a dual-threat response to Iranian naval provocations and North Korean missile tests. Maritime patrol aircraft (P-8 Poseidon, TEX2) and airborne early warning platforms (E-737) are conducting continuous surveillance in the Persian Gulf and South China Sea, likely in response to recent Iranian attacks on commercial shipping, including the MV Minoan Dignity incident. The presence of RAAF PC-21 training aircraft suggests ongoing allied exercises, possibly in preparation for joint operations. The VIP transport mission (B77W) indicates high-level coordination between U.S. military and diplomatic leadership. Collectively, the data reflects a U.S. strategy prioritizing maritime domain awareness, rapid response capabilities, and deterrence in critical theaters, with the Strait of Hormuz remaining a primary flashpoint due to its geopolitical and economic significance.</description>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>0,0,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
